    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2021-october/q4",
      "question": "<p>The curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\"></span> where</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^2+\\ln\\left(2x^2-4x+5\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>has a single turning point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\alpha\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> is a solution of the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2x^3-4x^2+7x-2=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>The iterative formula</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\frac17\\left(2+4x_n^{\\,2}-2x_n^{\\,3}\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>is used to find an approximate value for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>.</p><p>Starting with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=0.3\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>calculate, giving each answer to 4 decimal places,<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2\"></span></li><li>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_4\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol></li></ol><p>Using a suitable interval and a suitable function that should be stated,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> is 0.341 to 3 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
