    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2021-october/q11",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:75mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2021-october/q11-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2: the curve y = (ln x)^2 for x &gt; 0, falling steeply from near the y-axis to touch the x-axis and then rising; the region R between the curve and the x-axis from x = 2 to x = 4 is shaded.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of part of the curve with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=(\\ln x)^2\\qquad x&gt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The finite region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 2, is bounded by the curve, the line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\"></span>, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis and the line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\"></span></p><p>The table below shows corresponding values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>, with the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> given to 4 decimal places.</p><table class=\"practice-table\"><tr><td><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span></td><td>2</td><td>2.5</td><td>3</td><td>3.5</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span></td><td>0.4805</td><td>0.8396</td><td>1.2069</td><td>1.5694</td><td>1.9218</td></tr></table><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Use the trapezium rule, with all the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> in the table, to obtain an estimate for the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, giving your answer to 3 significant figures. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Use algebraic integration to find the exact area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, giving your answer in the form<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=a(\\ln 2)^2+b\\ln 2+c\" data-display=\"true\"></div>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are integers to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
